# CDK's DockerImageCode.fromImageAsset bundles the entire directory passed to it (the
# repo root, since the Lambda builder stage needs include/ and src/ from the main engine
# tree) as the Docker build context -- without this file, that includes build/ (CMake
# artifacts, including a full nested git checkout under _deps/), infra/cdk.out/ itself
# (recursively, compounding on every synth), and every node_modules/, none of which the
# Lambda image build needs. Found the hard way: cdk synth failed with ENAMETOOLONG from
# infra/cdk.out/ copying itself into itself repeatedly.
.git/
build/
infra/cdk.out/
infra/node_modules/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
**/__pycache__/
*.so
